<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tortosa</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dertosa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tortosa is a city on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarragona">Tarragona</a>, Catalonia, near the river's delta. Under Muslim rule it was a port and shipbuilding centre and the seat of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> kingdom, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramon-berenguer-iv-count-of-barcelona">Ramon Berenguer IV of Barcelona</a> conquered it in 1148 with Genoese help. Its Gothic cathedral and the Suda castle overlook the old town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tortosa.jpg" alt="Tortosa" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Hillewaert · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tortosa_(town_view).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Their towns included Hibera, near modern <b>Tortosa</b>, and they lived from farming, fishing and trade along the river and coast.</blockquote><a href="/state/ilercavones">Ilercavones</a></li><li><blockquote>Under al-Mundhir (1081-1090) it was joined with <b>Tortosa</b> and Dénia, and he allied with Barcelona against his brother al-Mutaman of Zaragoza, whose commander El Cid defeated them at Almenar in 1082.</blockquote><a href="/state/taifa-of-lerida">Taifa of Lérida</a></li><li><blockquote>At <b>Tortosa</b> the freedman Labib al-Amiri took power, reportedly for a time also sharing in the government of Valencia with Mubarak and Muzaffar.</blockquote><a href="/state/taifa-of-tortosa">Taifa of Tortosa</a></li><li><blockquote>Ahmad I al-Muqtadir (1046-1081) annexed <b>Tortosa</b> and Dénia and built the Aljafería palace.</blockquote><a href="/state/taifa-of-zaragoza">Taifa of Zaragoza</a></li></ul></section>
